content.text:
Players say Math Blitz gets too easy after five minutes, and when my niece plays she gets crushed by 12x12 multiplication. I want adaptive difficulty. Read docs/decisions/0001-game-architecture.md and the engine first.

Then compare three approaches:
(a) fixed levels with promotion and demotion rules;
(b) a staircase, the way hearing tests adapt: two right in a row makes it harder, one miss makes it easier;
(c) an Elo-style rating, where the player and each kind of question carry their own rating.

For each one: what state it needs, what we would have to tune, and how it behaves for a streaky player or one who gets tired. Recommend one, but don't implement it yet.

